            "review_text": "Ashley Nguyen\nLos Angeles, California2 contributions\n0\nA little taste of Saigon\nAug 2026 • Friends\nWe came to Com Tam 701 without expecting too much — just looking for a simple Vietnamese lunch in Saigon.\nThe grilled pork was the first thing we noticed. A little charred around the edges, and full of that sweet-savoury Vietnamese flavour. The broken rice was soft and fragrant, and with the fried egg, Vietnamese meatloaf, pickles and shredded pork, everything just worked together.\nAnd the fish sauce fried chicken rice was another delicious surprise. The chicken was perfectly golden and crispy, coated in a sweet and savory fish sauce glaze. It’s not necessarily a signature dish, but after trying it, I’d say it’s definitely worth ordering.\nWhat I liked most was that it didn’t feel like a “tourist version” of Vietnamese food. It felt simple, generous and comforting — the kind of meal you could imagine having on an ordinary day in Saigon.\nWe ended up staying longer than planned, just enjoying the food and the atmosphere.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nThe grilled pork broken rice is a must-try, and don’t overlook the fish sauce fried chicken rice. Portions are generous, so come hungry!\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten August 21, 2026",
