            "review_text": "Lannie Ngo\nGermany2 contributions\n0\nHidden away on the 7th floor\nAug 2026 • Couples\nIt was a bit of a hunt finding this place on the 7th floor of an old apartment building in District 1, but it was totally worth it. The spot is tiny and quiet, making you feel less like a tourist in a restaurant and more like a guest eating lunch at a local friend’s home. The owner is also super friendly and welcoming, which made the experience even better.\nI ordered the grilled pork belly with a fried egg. The pork was hot, smoky, and had just the right amount of fat to keep it juicy. The best part was breaking the runny egg yolk so it soaked right into the broken rice, mixed with green onions and little crunchy pieces of pork fat. Roused with a bit of sweet fish sauce and paired with the crunchy pickles, every bite was just super comforting.\nIf you like finding low-key, authentic local spots hidden away from the busy streets, this place is definitely a fun little find.\nRead more\nWritten August 16, 2026",
